  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "14. Objectives",
    "ruleNumber": "14.01",
    "summary": "A mission that uses objectives gives their locations on the deployment map. For a terrain objective, use the terrain area itself. Take measurements to or from the objective’s nearest point. Under the FAQ, an objective outside a terrain area is a 40mm objective marker centred on its location. Models may pass through a marker or finish a move on it. A marker’s range is 3 inches horizontally and 5 inches vertically, measured from its nearest point. See Level of Control for who holds an objective.",
